Sample bearing vibration data

This notice covers the files in these directories:
  data/real_bearings/
  data/signals/real_train/
  data/signals/real_test/
The MIT License in the LICENSE file at the root of this repository does not
apply to these files.

Data owner: Eric Bechhoefer
Original source: http://data-acoustics.com/measurements/bearing-faults/bearing-2/
Redistributed by The MathWorks, Inc. at
  https://github.com/mathworks/RollingElementBearingFaultDiagnosis-Data
  That repository holds the first four of the six folders of the original
  data set, reorganised into a training folder and a test folder.

License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

Changes made in this repository:
  data/real_bearings/ holds the MATLAB .mat files of the MathWorks
  repository, unmodified.
  data/signals/real_train/ and data/signals/real_test/ hold each recording
  converted to a CSV file with one column of acceleration values in g, and a
  JSON file with its sampling rate, signal unit, shaft speed, load, sample
  count, duration and bearing characteristic frequencies.
The converted files are shared under the same license, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

The data is provided as is, without warranties of any kind; the license
gives the full terms. Nothing in this notice implies endorsement by the data
owner or by The MathWorks, Inc.

The license does not permit commercial use. For commercial use of the data,
contact the data owner, as the MathWorks repository states.
